hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16524","Waki narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Rabiah al-Makhzumi narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, borrowed from him when he raided Hunayn thirty or forty thousand, and when he returned he repaid it to him, then he said: May Allah bless for you your family and your wealth, indeed the reward of a loan is repayment and praise."
